    "reason": "On the appended-corrections workload pinned answers with the default model were correct on 98.6% of reads versus 51.4% for query+reader and 79.2% for think, with 0% stale-wrong versus 48.6% and 20.8%. Mean freshness lag was 0.017 write batches versus 0.583 and 0.25. Zero leaks in 48 restricted-grant probes. Decision rule (set before the run): pinned beating query+reader on accuracy or freshness without leakage means default-on; it beats it on both."
  },
  "overall": "default_on",
  "default_decision": "Pinned questions ship on. The standing_questions phase, publishing and context_pack delivery of fresh pinned answers are on by default (cycle.standing_questions.enabled=true, publish_mode=publish). Pinning a question remains the consent for its paid refresh, as plan C1 specifies, so no pin is created automatically and a brain with no pins makes no model call. Migrated dream.auto_think questions keep their old enabled, budget and auto_commit state. No shipped default changes relative to run 1; the verdict label moves from opt_in to default_on.",
  "caveats": [
    "Retrieval asymmetry: the run-2 build anchors pinned refresh retrieval on the pin scope (entity page first, then pages that link to or name it, newest first). query+reader uses ordinary keyword query retrieval and think its own gather, both without that anchoring. The accuracy gap is partly this retrieval difference; a pin has a scope and an ad hoc query does not.",
    "Keyword-only retrieval for every arm: the harness brain has no embedding key.",
    "Cost: pinned with the default model costs more total dollars than query+reader until about 147 reads per pin (163 with the Sonnet refresh model). Per correct answer it costs 4.1x query+reader at 1 read per write, 0.59x at 10 and 0.24x at 100.",
    "Withdrawal is the weakest event: 1 of 6 (default model) and 2 of 6 (Sonnet) pinned answers missed the revert after forget in batch 7.",
    "Sonnet refresh returned non-JSON twice in 72 attempts (model_output_not_json); the pin kept its previous answer, which counts against it.",
    "One seed, 6 entities; dev stage."
  ],
